<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria Theresa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1717">1717</a>–<a href="/years/1780">1780</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Theresa was the only female ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands, inheriting them in 1740 under the Pragmatic Sanction. She lost most of Silesia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a> but held the rest, and reformed taxation, the army and schooling. She was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, and her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i-holy-roman-emperor">Francis I</a> and son Joseph II were emperors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-theresa.jpg" alt="Maria Theresa" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin van Meytens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaiserin_Maria_Theresia_(HRR).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
